WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:07.840
<i>Since the recent funeral we held for 
Harold Miller of the Kingdom of Soleil,</i>

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:06.860
<b>- November 24th -</b>

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.410
<i>in the northern part of the State of Theras,</i>

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.140
<i>not only have civilians begun to surrender,</i>

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.610
<i>but so too have the royal army soldiers.</i>

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.870
<i>This phenomenon is gradually spreading.</i>

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.870
<i>This is our chance to seize victory.</i>

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.620
<i>It's time to enact our planned 
full-scale offensive,</i>

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.290
<i>crush the Royal Army,</i>

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>and finally put an end to this war.</i>

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.630
I guess the propaganda actually worked, huh?

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.890
It won't matter here on the front lines.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.390
We're still being sent on these mop-up 
operations, losing people every day.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.770
If they're gonna do some big funeral, 
I wish they'd memorialize our guys, too.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.650
Hey, everyone... I had an idea.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:55.800
Next payday, why don't we send some money 
to the orphanage Commander Gail ran?

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.450
It's the least we can do to 
thank him for everything.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.560
Now there's a good idea!

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.660
Sure, I'm in.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:06.340
I don't buy much anyway, outside of booze.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.920
Give me a damned break.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.010
Paying obligations to a dead man...

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.260
What a bunch of self-congratulatory crap.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.990
Don't be that way. Just give a little bit.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.220
Really, Acting Commander Break?

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.270
Would that be an order, then?

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.770
That's enough out of you.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.900
I'm the one who's had enough.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.270
Get your heads out of your asses already!

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.700
How do you expect to fight like this?!

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.180
Withdraw! Withdraw!

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.570
We're on unfavorable ground!

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.040
They're gonna take us out!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.970
Break!

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.000
I'm still good!

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.300
You guys, withdraw!

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.540
You think you're hot stuff?!

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.340
Wait! Huey!

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.400
Huey, get back!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.980
You bastards!

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.150
The Price of Smiles

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.150
<i>The Price of Smiles</i>

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:43.410
<b><i>The Resolve of Two</i></b>

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.770
How'd it go?

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.570
I managed to pass it off 
as a broken transmitter.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.470
Excellent job back there, Acting Commander.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.770
What were you thinking?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.470
How could you do something so stupid?

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.220
Huh? My transmitter was broken, remember?

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.350
I'm being serious!

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.720
You could have died out there!

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.620
Chill out already.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.930
If anyone dies, they'll get replaced right away.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.720
Like how you became commander 
after the old man bit it!

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.230
You...

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.160
You little...

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.910
Doesn't it make you sad when 
you say things like that?

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.880
Let's do this...

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:36.820
Don't do it!

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:39.960
Stella!

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:41.960
Cut it out!

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.340
Guys, we don't need more problems right now!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.080
Hate to disappoint, but I'm not sad at all!

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.130
That's how war works! 
Didn't you get the memo?

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.100
Please, don't!

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.790
One minute you're smiling the day away,

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.470
the next you're all weepy and pissy.

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.690
You need psychiatric help, stat!

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.810
If we were that easily replaced,

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.240
Commander Gail wouldn't 
have died to protect us!

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.070
"Survive and see them through."

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:15.250
We're the only ones who got that order!

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:20.380
So from now on, I won't 
let one more of us die!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.390
You've got a serious screw loose.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.880
Huh? Why this orphanage?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.290
Someone from your squad have a kid there?

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.280
Why do you ask?

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.740
Well, Huey sent money to 
the same place earlier...

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.040
Honestly...

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:02.550
He has to make everything so difficult.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.820
My place...

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.470
Urgent message from Soleil!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.460
We have an urgent message from Soleil!

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:58.350
Gather at the rationing station!

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.980
Gather at the rationing station!

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:11.710
<i>Our nations have waged a long campaign now,</i>

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:14.240
<i>sacrificing many for our cause.</i>

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.230
<i>I will bring an end to all of that.</i>

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:25.210
<i>We've completed the new weapon 
we've been developing in secret.</i>

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:30.570
<i>It can destroy an Imperial 
battalion with ease.</i>

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:47.270
<i>I, Yuki Soleil, first princess of the 
Kingdom of Soleil, hereby declare:</i>

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:51.900
<i>I will do everything in my 
power to retake Hariant!</i>

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.840
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.070
<i>It's hard to believe this is 
the same Princess Yuki...</i>

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.540
<i>Was her earlier demeanor a ruse?</i>

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.640
We'll amass our main 
force in Hariant at once.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:13.030
Increase security on state borders, as well.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:13.620
Ma'am.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.060
I can't believe they cooked 
up a monster like that.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.040
I've heard our side's working hard on R&D, too,

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:24.850
but it really shows the difference 
in our tech levels...

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.990
<i>I won't let them die.</i>

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:32.680
Hey.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.700
All that big talk you were doing before...

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.890
It means you won't die, either, right?

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.080
Of course.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:46.080
Then, quit looking like a dead woman 
before we even get out there.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.590
We have our placement.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:02.350
<b>- December 5th -</b>

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:18.160
All forces, halt.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.120
Until we ascertain the range of 
their mobile artillery, stay put.

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:31.790
Looks like they're in a staring contest.

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:36.490
Never thought they'd send us to the 
polar opposite of the front line.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.140
Just how far away are we?

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.890
About 2,000 kilometers, looks like.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.410
Way too far away to join the main force... 
That's pretty "us," at least.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.490
Should we offer our gratitude 
to the old man up in heaven?

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.570
"We're living another day thanks to you."

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.780
I could beat you to within an inch of your life.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.640
You couldn't hit me unless 
it was a sucker punch.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.040
Are you guys going to keep doing this?

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.650
It never bothered me before now.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.050
But lately, your attitude has 
been getting under my skin.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.130
It's like looking at the way I used to be,

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.810
averting my eyes from something for so long.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.610
Is it, now?

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.250
<i>Buerger-3 to squad.</i>

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.310
<i>I've spotted an enemy squad.</i>

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.740
I'm tracking them now.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.590
Roger.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:44.950
We'll head out to support you now.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.870
Lily, be careful.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:50.960
<i>I will.</i>

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:53.630
Stella, moving out!

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:04.950
<i>I, Yuki Soleil, first princess of the 
Kingdom of Soleil, hereby declare:</i>

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:09.890
<b>- November 30th -</b>

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.890
<i>I will do everything in my 
power to retake Hariant!</i>

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.970
Have you gone mad?

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.640
What are you thinking?

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:19.730
We can't even deal with the 
surrendering civilian movement!

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:22.160
Yesterday, our recon squad

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.740
reported that the Empire is 
preparing a full-scale offensive.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.700
What?!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.830
This is our only remaining option.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:33.790
But do we stand a chance?

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:39.400
As discussed earlier, 
the completed mobile artillery

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.560
will help to compensate 
for our inferior numbers.

00:11:42.210 --> 00:11:45.870
And if we emphasize that it 
was Harold's final project,

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.210
it should raise the soldiers' morale.

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:56.300
Honestly... this is quite the 
plan you've come up with.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.690
The crucial part is yet to come.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.920
If the Senate knew what 
we were really planning,

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.930
they'd try to overturn us.

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:05.010
Yeah.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:08.070
I can't believe Miss Layla 
approved such an outrageous plan.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:14.830
I knew how long Princess Yuki had 
been torturing herself over it.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:21.340
Miss Layla, I've thought over again and again

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:26.310
that we should surrender to 
the Empire and end the war.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:31.290
But... even if we end this particular war,

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:34.650
the same thing will happen again someday.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:40.150
No... an even bigger war will take place,

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.490
and even more people might die.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.600
So I...

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:57.470
I want to shut down all 
the chrars on the planet.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:07.640
That's the answer you've 
come to, Princess Yuki?

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:15.120
I'm sorry to say, there's no way 
to make that happen from Soleil.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:21.730
But the data that Lord Izana 
sent us contained accounts

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.810
of an experimental facility 
in the old Verde Empire.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.660
An experimental facility?

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:32.020
The scientists of Verde once 
had the same idea you did.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:35.290
They constructed a facility 
to put it into practice.

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:41.920
At the time, they couldn't 
achieve their theorized result.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:48.450
But with the technology we have 
now, it might become possible.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:53.250
Miss Layla. Help me.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:02.830
Let's go over the plan one more time.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:05.570
First, in accordance with my declaration,

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.590
James will head towards Hariant with the 
main force and the mobile artillery.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:14.100
You should encounter the enemy 
somewhere in the State of North Robia.

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:15.680
Once they're in sight,

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:19.520
use the mobile artillery's range to fire 
a warning shot at their front line.

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.330
That will hold them in place.

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:25.670
Avoid an exchange of fire for as 
long as you can, and buy us time.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.580
If the enemy commander 
knows what they're doing,

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:32.430
a display of power like that 
should give them pause.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:38.510
But if they realize it's a 
hastily-prepared prototype...

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:39.450
Please.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:42.940
I've bluffed them on the 
battlefield enough times before.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.230
I'll make sure it works out.

00:14:47.890 --> 00:14:50.240
In the meantime, Miss Layla and I

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.180
will slip through the State of Theras, 
then the State of Chrisant,

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.100
on the way to old Verde Empire territory.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:00.640
To keep a low profile, our guard will 
be Yuni and Lune, and one other squad.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.450
When we arrive at the experimental facility...

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.760
Then...

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.660
Princess Yuki, I'm sure it will go well.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.730
"Passion and will!" Right?

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:33.810
You would not prefer to give it more time?

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:38.250
No... because I don't know 
if I'll ever make it back.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:42.790
Elisa is holding off, because I 
said I would tell her myself...

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:50.720
Princess Yuki, you're not 
here to eat dinner today?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:51.800
No.

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:54.160
Today, I came here to talk.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.380
About your papa.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:58.220
Papa? Is he coming home?

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.940
When? When's he coming home?!

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:03.930
Noel, listen to her.

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:06.230
Princess Yuki?

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:11.240
Noel...

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.460
You're lying!

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:20.910
Princess Yuki, why would you even say that?

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:22.640
Noel...

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.120
You're a liar, Princess Yuki!

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:28.090
Papa <i>is</i> coming home!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.700
He's coming home, right, Mama?

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.370
He's coming home!

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:36.600
Papa's coming home!

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:55.830
Princess Yuki.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:05.550
Let's go.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:19.640
Mobile artillery, prepare to fire.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.230
Preparing to fire.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:24.280
Get it as close as you 
can without hitting them.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.140
Yes, sir!

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:33.530
Range: 20 kilometers.

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:34.760
Locking on.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:36.910
Fire!

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.460
It's a hit.

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:57.630
Stay put for a while now, would you?

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.980
Now passing through northern 
State of Chrisant.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:16.610
The territory of the old Empire 
of Verde should be in sight soon.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.190
Don't let your guard down.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:19.990
You don't have to tell me that.

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:30.000
If Izana, Harold, and Joshua 
knew what I'm about to do...

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.170
Do you think they'd forgive me?

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:39.050
No matter what happens, 
I must accept sole responsibility.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.890
Because this is the decision I've made.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:51.770
I've felt the same fear 
you have, Princess Yuki.

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:56.330
When I lost my family in the 
accident twelve years ago,

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:59.210
I was assailed by unfathomable loneliness.

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:01.300
Miss Layla...

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:04.350
Even now, sometimes, when I look at you,

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:07.260
I'm reminded of my daughter.

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:09.160
Your daughter?

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:14.310
She was kind, and smiled, just like you.

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:25.310
Miss Layla... how did you get 
past the fear you felt then?

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:29.490
Your smile, Princess Yuki.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:47.200
Your smile has a mysterious power.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:52.370
That power that envelops 
people... it saved me.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.120
And that's when I decided...

00:19:56.480 --> 00:20:00.970
that no matter what happened, I would 
remain by that smile to the end.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:04.700
Miss Layla...

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:07.590
If all the chrars are shut down,

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:11.060
the people will face 
hardship like never before.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:14.450
That's when your role will truly begin.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:23.310
I will make my kingdom...

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:28.730
I will make everyone on this planet smile!

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.040
Yuki.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:41.990
If Mother had lived, do you think 
she would have done this for me?

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.550
Of course.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.940
Enemy approaching from eight o'clock!

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:55.440
We're being pursued!

00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:35.580
They're not the Order.

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:36.790
A margrave army, maybe?

00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:39.350
You think they're deserting?

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:42.040
That's old Verde territory ahead...

00:22:42.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We can't let them escape!

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:51.260
I guess we can't shake them off.

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:54.080
You go on. We'll hold them off.

00:22:54.080 --> 00:22:55.770
Thank you. Yuni?

00:22:56.120 --> 00:22:57.810
Understood. I'll be on standby.

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:02.730
Princess Yuki.

00:23:03.660 --> 00:23:05.200
Get away from the window.

00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:06.360
O-Okay.

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.040
Hey. Wasn't that...

00:23:16.300 --> 00:23:17.450
Damn it!

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.310
<b><i>The Price of Smiles</i></b>
